-- title:
--   Flatness at p under absolutely irreducible residual representation
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $N \geq 1$, and $S$ a finite set of natural numbers containing $p$ and every prime divisor of $N$. Let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero which is a domain with finite residue field and with $p$ in its maximal ideal, and let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathcal{O}'$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, together with the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$. Assume $p \nmid N$. Let $\rho$ be a [`GaloisRepAdic`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16) over $\mathcal{O}'$: a free $\mathcal{O}'$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal{O}'}(V)$ which is adically continuous, in the sense that for each $n$ some finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ has its pointwise stabiliser acting trivially on $V$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}^n V$. Assume: (i) the residual representation $\mathrm{ResidueField}(\mathcal{O}') \otimes_{\mathcal{O}'} V$ becomes irreducible after base change to an algebraic closure of the residue field, i.e. every Galois-stable submodule there is $\bot$ or $\top$; and (ii) for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^\ell$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ equals $X^2 - \chi(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Then $\rho$ is flat at $p$: the residue field of $\mathcal{O}'$ is finite and, for every ideal $I \subseteq \mathcal{O}'$ with $\mathcal{O}'/I$ finite, there is a commutative cocommutative Hopf algebra $H$ over the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ of fractions whose denominator is coprime to $p$, finite and flat over that subring, together with a bijection between the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $H$ (with their convolution group law) and $V/IV$ which is additive and intertwines the Galois action on points with the induced action of $\rho$ on $V/IV$.
--
--   This is the finite-flatness statement at the prime $p$ for the $p$-adic Galois representation cut out by a weight-two Hecke eigensystem of level prime to $p$, in the variant carrying the extra hypothesis that the residual representation is absolutely irreducible. It feeds the local conditions used later, being cited by [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.exists_pi_eq_and_isFlatAt_of_primeFactors_subset`](thm.html#CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.exists_pi_eq_and_isFlatAt_of_primeFactors_subset) and by the ordinariness statement [`CuspForm.isOrdinaryAt_of_point_of_isUnit_up_of_residual_isAbsolutelyIrreducible_of_residual_isOrdinaryAt`](thm.html#CuspForm.isOrdinaryAt_of_point_of_isUnit_up_of_residual_isAbsolutelyIrreducible_of_residual_isOrdinaryAt).
